Please provide information on what version(s) of aroma.affymetrix you
are using.  I strongly suspect that you have generated plots with two
different versions, is that correct?

For GLAD segmentation, it is always the 'SigmaC$Value' in the result
structure returned by glad() that is shown.  For other models, that is
currently only the CBS segmentation model, the standard deviation
estimate is the MAD of the first-order differences of the raw CNs
across the whole chromosome.  In aroma.affymetrix v0.9.0 and before
two estimates were displayed, namely the sample standard deviation and
the MAD of the raw CNs across the chromosome (not the first-order
difference).

BUG FIX: I just found a bug causing the sigma (and the chip type
annotation) not be displayed in the plots for non-GladModel (i.e. the
CbsModel).  You would get the error (although the graphs would still
be displayed/generated/saved):

  Plotting graph...
<simpleError in UseMethod("estimateStandardDeviation"): no applicable
method for "estimateStandardDeviation">

if you look at the verbose output.  I've committed a patch - to update do:

library(aroma.affymetrix)
downloadPackagePatch("aroma.affymetrix")

You know when it works again if you can do something like:

cbs <- CbsModel(cesFln)
plot(cbs, array=1, chromosome=19, verbose=-20)

without any errors being displayed.  I have also added a subscript
$\Delta$ to indicate that the estimate is based on the first-order
*differences*.

In other words, I would expect you to report that you don't see any
sigma:s at all for your most recent CbsModel graphs, if you run
aroma.affymetrix v0.9.1 (if not, please update).

/Henrik

