according to p24 of "Low Level Analysis of High-density
Oligonucleotide Array Data: Background, Normalization and
Summarization". Dissertation, Bolstad, BM.
before doing background correction, the low intensity signal is
corrected.
it has a parameter theta (its default value = 4).

I tried to adjust it, but I could not find suitable parameter in the
function RmaBackgroundCorrection.
how can I change the theta for background correction? or I have to do
it manually?

regards

J.

From u9dda904b2c7a149c at groups.google.com  Sun Apr 27 11:44:22 2008
From: u9dda904b2c7a149c at groups.google.com (Ken Simpson)
